Code":"direct-path","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/advaita"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/arsha-vidya","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/arsha-vidya","name":"Arsha Vidya","description":"Traditional teaching of Advaita Vedanta through the texts, in the line of Swami Dayananda Saraswati (Arsha Vidya Gurukulam, Q4796497).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"arsha-vidya","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/advaita"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/modern-nondual","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/modern-nondual","name":"Modern non-dual teachers","description":"Contemporary teachers of awakening who draw on Zen, Advaita and other sources without belonging to one lineage.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"modern-nondual","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/independent"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/plum-village","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/plum-village","name":"Plum Village","description":"Thich Nhat Hanh's Vietnamese Thiền community of engaged, mindful living.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"plum-village","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60763315"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/zen"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/soto-zen","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/soto-zen","name":"Sōtō Zen","description":"Dōgen's school of just-sitting (shikantaza); San Francisco Zen Center, Sanshin.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"soto-zen","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q749085"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/zen"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/rinzai-zen","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/rinzai-zen","name":"Rinzai Zen","description":"The koan school of Japanese Zen; Zen Studies Society.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"rinzai-zen","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q639625"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/zen"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/gelug","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/gelug","name":"Gelug","description":"The Tibetan school of Tsongkhapa, headed in practice by the Dalai Lamas.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"gelug","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q319218"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/tibetan"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese","name":"Burmese meditation lineages","description":"Myanmar's modern meditation schools: Mahasi noting, Pa-Auk samatha-vipassanā, U Ba Khin and Goenka.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"burmese","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/theravada"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/krishnamurti","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/krishnamurti","name":"Krishnamurti","description":"J. Krishnamurti's teaching after he left Theosophy in 1929: no path, no authority, freedom from the known.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"krishnamurti","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/independent"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/anandamayi-sangha","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/anandamayi-sangha","name":"Anandamayi Ma Sangha","description":"The ashrams and monastics around Anandamayi Ma (Shree Shree Anandamayee Sangha, Kankhal and Varanasi), devotional and non-sectarian.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"anandamayi-sangha","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hindu"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/divine-life-society","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/divine-life-society","name":"Divine Life Society","description":"The order founded by Swami Sivananda in Rishikesh, carried on by Swami Chidananda.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"divine-life-society","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/vedanta"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/siddha-yoga","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/siddha-yoga","name":"Siddha Yoga","description":"Guru-yoga path founded by Swami Muktananda in the line of Bhagawan Nityananda: shaktipat, chanting and meditation, drawing on Kashmir Shaiva texts.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"siddha-yoga","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3483106"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hindu"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/goenka-vipassana","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/goenka-vipassana","name":"Goenka Vipassana (U Ba Khin line)","description":"Lay Vipassana in the line of Ledi Sayadaw, Saya Thetgyi and U Ba Khin, taught by S. N. Goenka in 10-day dana-funded courses.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"goenka-vipassana","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kagyu","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kagyu","name":"Kagyu","description":"Tibetan school of the mahamudra lineage from Tilopa and Naropa through Marpa and Milarepa, led by the Karmapas.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"kagyu","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q471187"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/tibetan"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/nyingma","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/nyingma","name":"Nyingma","description":"The oldest Tibetan school, tracing to Padmasambhava, home of Dzogchen.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"nyingma","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q848771"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/tibetan"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sufism","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sufism","name":"Sufism","description":"The inner, mystical path of Islam: remembrance of God (dhikr), the master and the order, the poetry of love.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"sufism","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q9603"]},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/jewish","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/jewish","name":"Jewish mysticism","description":"Merkavah, Kabbalah, the Zohar and Hasidism: the contemplative and mystical currents of Judaism.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"jewish"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/philosophy-of-the-sacred","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/philosophy-of-the-sacred","name":"Philosophy of the sacred","description":"Contemporary philosophers and scientists on consciousness, meaning and the sacred: idealism, the divided brain, the meaning crisis, perennialism.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"philosophy-of-the-sacred"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/modern-paganism","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/modern-paganism","name":"Modern Paganism","description":"Druidry, Wicca, Heathenry and goddess spirituality: nature-centred traditions revived or founded in the modern era.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"modern-paganism","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q189753"]},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sikh","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sikh","name":"Sikhism","description":"The path of the ten Gurus and the Guru Granth Sahib: remembrance of the one Name, honest work and sharing.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"sikh","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q9316"]},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaivism","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaivism","name":"Śaivism","description":"Umbrella for Śiva-centred traditions: the ascetic Atimārga and the initiatory Mantramārga.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shaivism","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hindu"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/pashupata","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/pashupata","name":"Pāśupata (Atimārga)","description":"Earliest Śaiva ascetic order; ash, feigned madness, provoking censure.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"pashupata","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaiva-siddhanta","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaiva-siddhanta","name":"Śaiva Siddhānta","description":"Mainstream ritual Śaivism of the Mantramārga; Sanskrit āgamas, later the Tamil Śaiva temple tradition. Kauai Aadheenam teaches a monistic form.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shaiva-siddhanta","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/trika","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/trika","name":"Trika","description":"Abhinavagupta's synthesis around the Mālinīvijayottara; Tantrāloka.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"trika","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kashmir-shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/pratyabhijna","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/pratyabhijna","name":"Pratyabhijñā (Recognition)","description":"Philosophical school: liberation as recognising oneself as Śiva.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"pratyabhijna","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kashmir-shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/spanda","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/spanda","name":"Spanda (Vibration)","description":"Śiva Sūtras and Spanda Kārikās: consciousness as pulsation.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"spanda","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kashmir-shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/krama","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/krama","name":"Krama / Kālīkula (Mahārtha)","description":"Kālī-centred phases (krama) of cognition; Twelve Kālīs.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"krama","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kashmir-shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaktism","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaktism","name":"Śāktism","description":"Goddess-centred traditions; parent of Kaula, Śrī Vidyā and Kālī lines.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shaktism","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hindu"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shakta","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shakta","name":"Śākta practice (Kālī, Kāmākhyā, Bhairavī)","description":"Bucket for living goddess practice not tied to a single classical school (Kāmākhyā upāsanā, Linga Bhairavi, Daśa Mahāvidyā).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shakta","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaktism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sri-vidya","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sri-vidya","name":"Śrī Vidyā","description":"Worship of Lalitā Tripurasundarī through the Śrī Chakra and the fifteen-syllable mantra.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"sri-vidya","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaktism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/siddha-siddhanta","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/siddha-siddhanta","name":"Nāth / Siddha Siddhānta","description":"Nāth yogī order (Gorakhnāth); Siddha Siddhānta Paddhati; alchemy and haṭha.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"siddha-siddhanta","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaivism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hatha","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hatha","name":"Haṭha Yoga (premodern)","description":"Physical-yogic methods first set out in Vajrayāna and Śaiva circles (Amṛtasiddhi, Dattātreyayogaśāstra, Haṭhapradīpikā).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"hatha","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/siddha-siddhanta"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/tantra-studies","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/tantra-studies","name":"Tantra studies (academic)","description":"Not a tradition: a field tag for scholarly lectures (philology, history).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"tantra-studies","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/hindu"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/chah-line","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/chah-line","name":"Ajahn Chah line (Wat Nong Pah Pong)","description":"Includes Amaravati, Chithurst/Cittaviveka, Abhayagiri, Bodhinyana/BSWA, Wat Pah Nanachat, Wat Marp Jan, Wat Boonyawad, Tisarana, Birken.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"chah-line","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/thai-forest"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/mun-boowa-line","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/mun-boowa-line","name":"Dhammayut forest line (Ajahn Mun → Maha Boowa / Ajaan Lee)","description":"Note: Ajahn Dtun, listed by the brief under this line, was ordained by Ajahn Chah (Mahānikāya) and is filed under chah-line.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"mun-boowa-line","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/thai-forest"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/mahasi","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/mahasi","name":"Mahasi method (noting)","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"mahasi","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/pa-auk","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/pa-auk","name":"Pa-Auk (samatha-first, Abhidhamma)","description":"The Burmese system taught by Pa-Auk Sayadaw from the Visuddhimagga and Abhidhamma: deep jhāna first, usually through mindfulness of breathing, then insight into mind and matter, their causes across past and future lives, and dependent origination.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"pa-auk","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/mogok","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/mogok","name":"Mogok Sayadaw (dependent origination)","description":"Official channel is Burmese-language only; no English clips.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"mogok","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shwe-oo-min","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shwe-oo-min","name":"Shwe Oo Min (natural awareness)","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shwe-oo-min","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/burmese"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sri-lankan","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sri-lankan","name":"Sri Lankan Theravāda (forest & scholastic)","description":"Hillside Hermitage is already deep in app (early-suttas).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"sri-lankan","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/theravada"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/buddhist-studies","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/buddhist-studies","name":"Buddhist studies (academic)","description":"Scholarly lineage node: edges are academic_supervisor_of.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"buddhist-studies","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/buddhism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/chinmaya-mission","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/chinmaya-mission","name":"Chinmaya Mission","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"chinmaya-mission","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/advaita"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sivananda-yoga","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sivananda-yoga","name":"Sivananda Yoga Vedanta Centres","description":"Swami Vishnudevananda's international centres teaching his guru Sivananda's yoga.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"sivananda-yoga","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2369406"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/divine-life-society"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/bihar-yoga","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/bihar-yoga","name":"Bihar School of Yoga (Satyananda Yoga)","description":"Yoga of Swami Satyananda, disciple of Sivananda, and the Bihar School of Yoga.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"bihar-yoga","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.