ion/hindu"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/transcendental-meditation","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/transcendental-meditation","name":"Transcendental Meditation","description":"Mantra meditation of Maharishi Mahesh Yogi.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"transcendental-meditation","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q558571"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/vedanta"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/swedenborgian","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/swedenborgian","name":"Swedenborgianism","description":"Thought and church following the visions of Emanuel Swedenborg.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"swedenborgian","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1755789"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/esoteric"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/spiritualism","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/spiritualism","name":"Spiritualism","description":"Movement based on communication with the dead through mediums.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"spiritualism","sameAs":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q829348"],"broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/esoteric"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kaula","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kaula","name":"Kaula / Kula","description":"Clan (kula) cults of yoginīs and Bhairava; source of many later Śākta and haṭha practices.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"kaula","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shaktism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/franciscan-contemplative","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/franciscan-contemplative","name":"Franciscan contemplative","description":"The Franciscan contemplative current: poverty and minority as a way of seeing, from Francis and Clare through Bonaventure to today.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"franciscan-contemplative","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/christian"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/lurianic","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/lurianic","name":"Lurianic Kabbalah","description":"The Kabbalah of Isaac Luria as recorded by Hayyim Vital: contraction (tzimtzum), the breaking of the vessels, and repair (tikkun).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"lurianic","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/kabbalah"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/chishti","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/chishti","name":"Chishti order","description":"The Sufi order of Muinuddin Chishti, rooted in Ajmer: music (sama, qawwali), service of the poor, and love of the teacher.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"chishti","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sufism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/qadiri","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/qadiri","name":"Qadiri order","description":"The Sufi order of Abdul Qadir Gilani of Baghdad: sober adherence to the law joined to inward poverty and reliance on God.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"qadiri","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/sufism"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/learned-magic","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/learned-magic","name":"Learned magic","description":"Renaissance learned magic: Ficino's Neoplatonic natural magic, Agrippa's three books, Dee's angelic conversations, Bruno's heroic frenzies. Studied, not practised, here.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"learned-magic","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/esoteric"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shamanic","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shamanic","name":"Shamanic traditions","description":"Shamanic and plant-medicine healing traditions of the Americas, entered only where lineage, teachers and screening are verifiable.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shamanic"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/santo-daime","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/santo-daime","name":"Santo Daime","description":"Syncretic Amazonian religion founded by Raimundo Irineu Serra (1930s): Christianity, South American shamanism, African animism, Kardecist spiritism. Legal churches in Oregon, Los Angeles, Washington.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"santo-daime","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/christian"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/udv","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/udv","name":"União do Vegetal (UDV)","description":"Christian Spiritist religion founded by José Gabriel da Costa; hoasca sacrament; US Supreme Court exemption 2006 (Gonzales v. O Centro). Núcleos across the US.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"udv","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/christian"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shipibo-curanderismo","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shipibo-curanderismo","name":"Shipibo curanderismo","description":"Shipibo-Conibo plant-spirit healing (curanderismo): onanya healers, ikaros songs, dietas. Entered via its longest-running centre, not via individual claims.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"shipibo-curanderismo","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/shamanic"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/jain","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/jain","name":"Jainism","description":"The Jain dharma: non-violence (ahimsa), non-possessiveness and many-sidedness (anekantavada) on the tirthankara path.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"jain"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/taoist","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/taoist","name":"Taoism","description":"The Chinese Way: Daodejing and Zhuangzi, inner alchemy, ritual and martial lineages (Quanzhen, Zhengyi, Wudang).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"taoist"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/bahai","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/bahai","name":"Baha'i Faith","description":"The Baha'i Faith: unity of God, religion and humanity; no clergy, elected assemblies; Houses of Worship open to all.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"bahai"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/african-diaspora","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/african-diaspora","name":"African diaspora religions","description":"African diaspora religions of the Americas, entered only via heritage-listed houses with published contacts.","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"african-diaspora"},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/candomble","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/candomble","name":"Candomblé","description":"Ketu-nation Candomblé of Bahia: orixá worship, entered via the IPHAN-listed Ilê Axé Opô Afonjá (1910).","inDefinedTermSet":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/","termCode":"candomble","broader":{"@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/african-diaspora"}},{"@type":"DefinedTerm","@id":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/native-american-church","url":"https://tantrafiles.xyz/tradition/native-american-church","name":"Native American Church","description":"The peyote way of the North American tribes; pan-tribal church body (NACNA). Tribally roote